      "body": "# Commit process CAS renames with the work\n\n## Requirement\nWhen `zqk` creates or updates an instance under `docs/process/` (not `_internal/`),\nthe write is a content-addressed **rename**: old 64-hex YAML deleted, new hash\nuntracked, same YAML `id:`.\n\nAgents MUST stage that delete+add pair **in the same git commit** as the code\n(or other work) that caused the object change. Do not land code while\n`complete` / `in_progress` YAML stays untracked.\n\n## Mechanical gate\n`scripts/check-process-cas-commit-with-work.sh` runs from\n`tools/git-hooks/pre-commit` and `scripts/git-commit-as-agent.sh`.\nIf a commit is staged and an unstaged CAS rename pair exists for the same `id:`,\nthe commit fails.\n\nBreak-glass **this commit only**: `ZQK_ALLOW_UNSTAGED_PROCESS_CAS=1`.\n\n## Do not\n- `git restore` / `git checkout --` / `git clean` under `docs/process/` to tidy\n  untracked hash YAML (kernel state, not junk).\n- Treat Cursor `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` as the authoring plane for this rule.\n\n## Parent\nCLI-only instance edits: `POL-ONBOARD-001`. Vocabulary: glossary term\n**process data**.\n",
      "category": "workflow",
      "context": "CLI writes hash-named YAML under docs/process/ before git commit. Leaving the\ncomplete/in_progress rename untracked, then git reset --hard origin/main,\nrestores the old planned file and completed kernel work looks demoted.\nCursor .mdc prose is not SSOT (POL-AGENT-001 kernel-first).\n",
      "created_at": "2026-08-19T00:53:59Z",
      "created_by": "ACC-1785920548450214012-68b850c0",
      "id": "POL-CODE-CAS-COMMIT-001",
