      "id": "ASK-1785642073632982000-e7c81062",
      "instructions": "Filesystem twin (keep in sync): `.zqk/skills/scheduler-expert/SKILL.md` (and `skills/scheduler-expert/`).\nSeal/refresh tracking: [REDACTED-ID] / [REDACTED-ID].\n\n# ZQK Scheduler Expert\n\n## Hard rules for agents\n\n| Do | Do not |\n|----|--------|\n| `zqk scheduler scan-tests --package ./…` for package gates | Foreground `go test ./…` / multi-minute waits |\n| Record **job id + log path**, continue work | Poll/`sleep` the session waiting for bundles |\n| Prefer targeted bundles over `--all` | Spam scan-tests in tight loops |\n| Rebuild `bin/zqk` when jobs exec the CLI | Assume daemon picked up unbuilt code |\n\nLong-lived: `zqk scheduler start`, `zqk mcp daemon`, **`zqk feed watch`** (timeout hook treats these as daemons — do not rely on default ~2m auto-timeout).\n\n## Core patterns\n\n1. **Pipeline init** — extend scheduler startup stages; don’t bolt side paths onto bootstrap.\n2. **Handlers** — `RunWrapperHandler` / typed handlers; idempotent; honor `context.Done()`.\n3. **Concurrency** — use project `goroutinelabels` / structured patterns; no naked `go func()` in production paths.\n4. **CAS + runtime delta for `scheduler_job`** — not `stream_current` as authority (see `FILESYSTEM_DATA_LAYOUT.md`).\n5. **Policies** — scheduler `PolicyEngine` decides job execute/skip/defer; POL-* objects are agent/coding constraints (different layer).\n\n## Ops cheatsheet\n\n```bash\n./bin/zqk scheduler start          # or ensure-scheduler-running.sh\n./bin/zqk scheduler scan-tests --package ./pkg/vds\n./bin/zqk scheduler activity\n./bin/zqk scheduler test-failures\n./bin/zqk scheduler history --job-id SCH-run-bundle-0\n```\n\nLogs: `.zqk/logs/scheduler/` (test-bundles / cvs paths per install).\n\n## Done claims\n\nScheduler green ≠ product done. Pair bundle evidence with **VDS** (`zqk workflow vds evaluate`) when claiming BLI/CVS progress.\n\n## References\n\n- `.cursor/rules/tests-background-output-to-file.mdc`\n- `scripts/scheduler/README.md`, `scripts/README.md`\n- `.zqk/skills/zqk-expert/SKILL.md` (swarm operating digest)\n",
      "instructions_summary": "Scheduler scan-tests, bundles, daemon ops, long-lived feed watch.",
